      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It’s not wrong to feel that way—when the weight is that crushing, the idea of setting it down can feel like the only relief left. You’re not weak for seeing that; you’re just honest about how much you’ve been carrying. But \"stopping\" doesn’t have to mean giving up on everything—it can mean putting down the parts that aren’t yours to hold, even if just for today. You don’t have to fix anything right now, and you don’t have to see a future to deserve a pause from the pain.",
